#pragma once

// GENERATED by tools/config_inventory.py --emit-header. Do not edit by hand.
//
// Every XML attribute name the loader reads anywhere. It exists so a config can be checked
// for names that are not read by anything: pugixml ignores unknown attributes silently, which
// is how `GBMSigma` stayed in a dozen configs and in the parameter reference for months while
// being read by nothing at all.
//
// It includes names read by the VALIDATOR rather than by the engine. Both sides parse the
// same XML, so the engine ignoring an attribute does not make it dead: `scaleR` is read only
// in Python and reaches a Grafana panel from there. The generator scans both trees, so this
// needs no hand-kept exception list.
//
// The set is flat rather than per element. Element attribution is derived from which source
// file performs the read, so an attribute a class reads off its own child node is filed under
// the parent, and a per-element check would report those as errors on every run. A warning
// that is wrong even occasionally gets ignored, so this deliberately catches only the case it
// can be certain about: a name nothing reads. Making attribution exact would let this tighten
// to per element, and that is the upgrade path.

